onchipmem.resource/--background--           onchipmem.resource/--background--

   PURPOSE
     The onchipmem.resource provides access to the On Chip Memory (OCM) 
     found on the APM460Ex SoC (used on the Sam460ex board for example).

     The OCM buffer is 64KB in size, 128-bit bus width, and is much faster 
     than main RAM, up to double the DDR2 speed, basically it has a speed 
     similar to the 460Ex L2 cache.

     It's main use is to store often accessed application data, or as a way 
     to trasfer more quicly a data buffer to/from video ram for example.

   NOTES
     this 64KB buffer is located outside the 2GB addressable space used by 
     AmigaOS 4, there may be some system function which doesn't like to be 
     passed an adrees beyound this limit, take care.

     Never use CopyMem or CopyMemQuick from exec.library, but use
     CopyOnChipMem instead.

onchipmem.resource/CopyOnChipMem             onchipmem.resource/CopyOnChipMem

   NAME
     CopyOnChipMem -- optimized memory copy function from/to OCM

   SYNOPSIS
     CopyOnChipMem( Source, Destination, Size )

     void CopyOnChipMem( ULONG *, ULONG *, ULONG );

   FUNCTION
     CopyOnChipMem is a highly optimized memory copy function, with
     restrictions on the size and alignment of its arguments: if one of the 
     used buffers is in main RAM, it's assumed to have been allocated with 
     AVT_Contiguous=TRUE, AVT_PhysicalAlignment=8 or higher and 
     AVT_Lock=TRUE.
     Source or destination (not both) must reside in OCM, in addition, 
     the size must be a multiple of 8.

     Arbitrary overlapping copies are not supported.

     The internal implementation of this function will change from
     system to system, and may be implemented via hardware DMA.

   INPUTS
     Source            a pointer to the source data region
     Destination       a pointer to the destination data region
     Size              the size (in bytes) of the memory area. Zero copies
                       zero bytes

   NOTES
     avoid to use the On Chip Memory buffer with device drivers.

onchipmem.resource/ObtainOnChipMem         onchipmem.resource/ObtainOnChipMem

   NAME
     ObtainOnChipMem -- Obtain access to OnChip RAM.

   SYNOPSIS
     Address = ObtainOnChipMem( )

     ULONG * ObtainOnChipMem( void );

   FUNCTION
     Acquires exclusive access to the 460ex onchip ram.

   RESULTS
     Address           Pointer to the 64KB OnChip RAM  buffer.

   NOTES
     Never assume the returned pointer address to be always the same.

onchipmem.resource/ReleaseOnChipMem       onchipmem.resource/ReleaseOnChipMem

   NAME
     ReleaseOnChipMem -- Allow OnChip Ram to others.

   SYNOPSIS
     ReleaseOnChipMem( )

     void ReleaseOnChipMem( void );

   FUNCTION
     Relinquish exclusive access to the 460ex OnChip Ram.

